ca-pub-9762662687323163\" data-ad-format=\"auto\" data-ad-slot=\"7596594071\" data-full-width-responsive=\"true\" style=\"display:block\"></ins>\n<script type=\"13dbc27ad2c4c4476365963b-text/javascript\">\n     (adsbygoogle = window.adsbygoogle || []).push({});\n</script>\n<div class=\"gb-container gb-container-ec1f6e4c\">\n<h6 class=\"gb-headline gb-headline-c7683bda gb-headline-text\">Bihar BPSC Special School Teacher Recruitment 2025 : Vacancy Details</h6>\n<div class=\"gb-headline gb-headline-60ccea19 gb-headline-text\"><table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%;\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 17.9403%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>Post Name</strong></span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 15.4294%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>No. Of Post</strong></span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 66.6302%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>Eligibility Criteria</strong></span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 17.9403%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Special School Teacher (Class 1 to 5)</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 15.4294%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">5334</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 66.6302%;\">\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Candidates should have achieved a minimum of 50% in their higher secondary (10+2) or an equivalent exam. and</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Candidates must possess a valid CRR number from the Rehabilitation Council of India and have completed a D.El.Ed. in Special Education from a Council-recognized institution. Or</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Candidates must have a D.El.Ed. or an equivalent Diploma in Special Education from a Rehabilitation Council of India-recognized institution, along with a valid CRR (Central Rehabilitation Register) number issued by the Council. Or</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Six months of specialized training in the field of cross-disability. Or</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Must have successfully passed the BSSTET Paper I Exam under the Special School Teacher Eligibility Test, 2023.</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Must be a citizen of India.</span></li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 17.9403%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Special School Teacher (Class 6 to 8)</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 15.4294%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">1745</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 66.6302%;\">\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Candidates having Graduation degree with a minimum of 50% marks from a recognized university.</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">A valid CRR (Central Rehabilitation Register) number issued by the Rehabilitation Council of India, along with a B.Ed. in Special Education from an institution recognized by the Council. Or</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">A Certificate or Diploma in Special Education along with a B.Ed., considered equivalent to a B.Ed. in Special Education by the Rehabilitation Council of India (RCI), from an RCI-recognized institution, and a valid CRR number issued by the RCI. Or</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Six months of specialized training in the field of cross-disability. Or</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Must have successfully passed the BSSTET Paper I Exam under the Special School Teacher Eligibility Test, 2023.</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Must be a citizen of India.</span></li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>\u00a0</p>\n<table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%;\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 100%;\">\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\"><strong><span style=\"color: #800000;\">You May Also Check :</span></strong> <a href=\"https://sarkariresult.com.cm/rajasthan-high-court-class-vi-employees-peon-recruitment-2025/\"><strong>Rajasthan High Court Class VI Employees Peon Recruitment 2025</strong></a></span></li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>\u00a0</p>\n<table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%;\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 100%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"background-color: #000080; color: #ffffff; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>\u00a0How To Check &amp; Download Bihar BPSC Special School Teacher Final Answer Key 2026\u00a0</strong></span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 100%;\">\n<ul>\n<li data-end=\"414\" data-start=\"335\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Visit the <strong data-end=\"411\" data-start=\"345\">official website of the Bihar Public Service Commission (BPSC)</strong>.</span></li>\n<li data-end=\"501\" data-start=\"418\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">On the homepage, go to the <strong data-end=\"490\" data-start=\"445\">Answer Key / Model Answer / Notifications</strong> section.</span></li>\n<li data-end=\"582\" data-start=\"505\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Look for the link titled <strong data-end=\"580\" data-start=\"530\">\u201cBPSC Special School Teacher Final Answer Key 2026.\u201d</strong></span></li>\n<li data-end=\"644\" data-start=\"586\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Click on the <strong>Final</strong> <strong data-end=\"613\" data-start=\"599\">Answer Key</strong> link when it becomes active.</span></li>\n<li data-end=\"693\" data-start=\"648\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">The final answer key will open in <strong data-end=\"690\" data-start=\"676\">PDF format</strong>.</span></li>\n<li data-end=\"761\" data-start=\"697\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Download the PDF of the final answer key and save it to your device.</span></li>\n<li data-end=\"847\" data-start=\"765\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Compare your marked final answers with the official key to estimate your expected score.</span></li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>\u00a0</p>\n